                  DIGITAL DLT TAPE SUBSYSTEM FAMILY
      TO BE SUPPORTED BY IBM ADSTAR DISTRIBUTED STORAGE MANAGER


  Increased Flexibility and Reliability for Desktop and Workstation
                   Users in Networked Environments


MAYNARD, Mass., March 20, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that its DLT tape subsystems family will be 
supported by ADSTAR Distributed Storage Manager (ADSM) for AIX, 
Version 2.1. IBM's ADSM software provides automated distributed 
storage management, including back-up and recovery, archiving, and 
hierarchical storage management (HSM) in heterogeneous computing 
environments with desktop to data center scalability.

     "By providing support for StorageWorks we are visibly 
broadening the choice of storage subsystems for our ADSM customers" 
said Nora Denzel, director of storage software products, IBM Storage 
Systems Division.

     ADSM software support will be available in the second quarter 
of 1996 by PTF update for Digital's TZ87, TZ87N, TZ875, TZ877, 
TZ877N, SXTL-Bn, TZ88, TZ885, TZ887 and SWXTL-Cn Tape Drive Families 
on the AIX platform. IBM plans also to extend this support of 
Digital's DLT loaders on additional ADSM servers including OS/2 and 
SUN.

     Digital's DLT loaders offer unattended backup with industry-
leading capacities (20GB or 40GB per cartridge with compression) and 
high performance (up to 7GB/hour) with up to 2.5 MB/s sustained data 
transfer rate.  Package options include the tabletop and 
StorageWorks building block drives, 5 and 7 cartridge loaders for 
Digital systems and other leading system manufacturers.

     "IBM's support of StorageWorks will enable AIX users to take 
full advantage of the modular, scalable design of the StorageWorks 
product line when using ADSM storage management software," said 
Robert Rennick, vice president and general manager, Storage Business 
Unit, Digital Equipment Corporation.

     StorageWorks products are available on multiple operating 
systems and hardware platforms, including Digital, Hewlett-Packard, 
IBM and Sun servers and workstations, and Novell and Windows NT 
environments. Products are available through DECdirect, Digital's 
business partners and local Digital sales offices.  For more 
information about Digital's complete line of hardware and software 
products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) or visit 
http://www.storage.digital.com/ on the World Wide Web.  For more 
information about IBM ADSTAR Distributed Storage Manager, call 
1-800-IBM-3333 (ask for STAR 20) or visit 
http://www.storage.ibm.com/storage/software/adsm/adsmhome.htm .

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global market-place.
