                DIGITAL 64-BIT ALPHASTATIONS TO POWER
                   AIR FORCE WORKSTATION CONTRACT

                                  
MAYNARD, Mass., March 22, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today announced that its 64-bit Alpha workstations have been 
selected as the platform of choice for the U.S. Air Force 
workstation contract.  Under the terms of the Indefinite Delivery, 
Indefinite Quantity (IDIQ) contract, Digital will supply as many as 
37,000 Alpha workstations as a subcontractor to Hughes Data Systems, 
the prime contractor.  Air Force workstations is a dual award 
contract with Sun Microsystems being the other prime contractor.  
The value of the contract could total more than $956 million over 
seven years.

     The contract provides for workstations, peripherals, software, 
services and support.  The U.S. Air Force's Electronic Systems 
Center, located at Hanscom Air Force Base in Bedford, Massachusetts, 
is the procurement agency for the contract.

     The Alpha workstations will run the latest release of Digital's 
industry-leading 64-bit operating system, Digital UNIX(R) Version 
4.0.  The many new features of this release include case-of-use 
enhancements, greater application portability, networking 
advancements, and overall performance and scalability improvements.

     "The mission-critical nature of Air Force operations demands 
powerful performance at price points that satisfy budget 
requirements," said Jim O'Neill, vice president and general manager 
of Digital's Federal Government Region.  "Coupled with Hughes' 
integration expertise, the scalability and price/performance of 
Digital's family of 64-bit products provide the Air Force with a 
solution set to achieve organizational objectives.  This contract 
award is a major endorsement for the next generation 64-bit Alpha 
technologies.  We applaud the Air Force for its vision."

     "Digital's industry-leading Alpha processor family, mature 
64-bit operating systems, and very attractive prices were key to 
this highly competitive award," said E. O. Knowles, president of 
Hughes Data Systems.

     Hughes Data Systems, located in Irvine, California, is a unit 
of Hughes Aircraft Company.  Hughes Data Systems has been providing 
commercial computers and integration services to government agencies 
for the past five years.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
                                ####

