   DIGITAL AND CYBERCASH CREATE PREMIER INTERNET COMMERCE SOLUTION


     Companies Announce Plans to Integrates CyberCash Technology
                        with Server Solution


NEW YORK, NY, March 25, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and 
CyberCash, Inc., a leading developer of secure Internet payment 
solutions, today announced plans to incorporate Cybercash technology 
with Digital Internet products.  Digital intends to offer the 
CyberCash CashRegister Merchant Solution and CyberCash Wallet as 
part of Alpha Internet commerce solutions, to enable secure 
electronic commerce on the Internet. The announcement was made at 
the Internet and Electronic Commerce Expo.

     "Combining CyberCash's expertise in electronic payments with 
Digitals high performance Alpha platform provides a perfect solution 
for businesses interested in Internet commerce, "said Magdalena 
Yesil, co-founder and vice president, marketing and technology 
industries, CyberCash.  "CyberCash is excited to work with Digital.
     
Paving the Way for Electronic Commerce Solutions

     "Digital is partnering with the premier application leaders in 
electronic commerce such as CyberCash, to deliver a breadth of 
commerce solutions," said Rose Ann Giordano, vice president of 
Digital's Internet Business Group.  "Digital's high-performance 
Alpha system offers businesses an industrial strength, scalable 
solution that optimizes application performance as a company grows."

     The technology provided by CyberCash and Digital is intended to 
offer customers a complete and real time merchant system for secure, 
high-volume transactions over the Internet.  Digital intends to 
offer the CyberCash Wallet and CashRegister with Digital Alpha 
Internet server solutions to enable full scale electronic commerce 
over the Internet.  CyberCash Wallet and CashRegister will be 
available to the existing Digital customer base and will be 
available from both the CyberCash and Digital World Wide Web sites.

Using CyberCash

     The CyberCash Wallet gives consumers the instantaneous ability 
to pay for goods or services received from merchants on the World 
Wide Web, and provides secure communication between the consumer, 
the CyberCash merchant and the bank.  The CyberCash Wallet is a free 
software program that is installed on a consumers personal computer 
and allows CyberCash transactions to move between a merchant's 
server and the bank transaction server system.  The CyberCash Wallet 
has the graphical look and feel of a real wallet and supports any 
number of credit cards including Visa, MasterCard, Discover and 
American Express.

     The CyberCash CashRegister, a secure Merchant payment Service, 
provides software integration modules into a server platform which 
accept payments made with the CyberCash Wallet over the Internet and 
to receives the information necessary to processing a credit card, 
electronic check or coin transaction.  The CyberCash system is 
designed to build on, and to be compatible with, existing financial 
institution infrastructure, and allows CyberCash merchants to 
process transactions with US credit card processors.
   
About CyberCash, Inc.

     CyberCash, Inc. of Reston, Virginia, founded in August 1994, is 
a leading developer of software and service solutions for secure 
financial transactions over the Internet.  The CyberCash system is 
designed to allow banks to offer secure Internet payments to their 
merchants. CyberCash works with virtually all credit card processing 
institutions, enabling payments by credit card, electronic check and 
electronic coin to be instantaneously processed. The CyberCash 
System includes Consumer software,  Merchant software, and Gateway 
Services and it operates with most Internet browsers and operating 
systems and server platforms.  The company's initial service, which 
handles payments using most major credit cards, was introduced in 
April 1995.

About Digital Equipment Corporation

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
