         DIGITAL AND OPEN MARKET TO DELIVER SECURE INTERNET
                         BUSINESS SOLUTIONS


       Merchant Solution and OM-Axcess Packaged With Digital's
                       Alpha Internet Servers


NEW YORK, New York, March 26, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Open Market, Inc., a leading provider of electronic commerce and 
enterprise-wide applications for the Internet, today announced plans 
to incorporate Open Markets technology into Digitals Internet 
products.  Through a technology agreement, Digital will offer Open 
Markets Merchant Solution and OM-Axcess software with its Alpha 
Internet commerce offerings, to enable merchants to securely run 
their businesses on the World Wide Web.  The announcement was made 
at the Internet and Electronic Commerce Expo.

     Merchant Solution is the first complete business solution that 
allows merchants to securely run their business on the Web.  
OM-Axcess is configurable software that enables a company to 
centrally manage secure access to content distributed across 
multiple servers.  Merchant Solution is available immediately with 
Digital's Internet commercial offerings.  OM-Axcess will be 
available at the end of April with these offerings.

     "We are pleased to be able to partner with a company like 
Digital to further promote secure Internet commerce," said Gary 
Eichhorn, CEO of Open Market. "By bundling these products, we're 
jointly providing a mission-critical platform for companies to run 
their business and Intranet applications on the World Wide Web."

Premier Internet Commerce Solutions

     "Combining Open Market's Internet Commerce applications with 
the high performance of the Digital Alpha Server platform provides a 
perfect solution for businesses interested in full-scale electronic 
commerce on the Internet," said Rose Ann Giordano, Vice President of 
Digital's Internet Business Group. "Customers will benefit from this 
partnership through our delivery of secure, robust Internet and 
Intranet solutions."

     Founded in 1994, Open Market, Inc. offers a full spectrum of 
high-performance business software products on the Internet. These 
products are revolutionary in their architecture, breadth, and 
functionality and enable companies to re-invent the way they do 
business in the information economy.  Open Market's software 
products bring the full range of business capability to the Internet 
and make enterprise-wide applications, secure electronic commerce, 
and industry-specific solutions possible.  The company, 
headquartered in Cambridge, Mass., can be reached at 617-621-9500 or 
on the World Wide Web at http://www.openmarket.com.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.  The company, headquartered 
in Maynard, Mass. can be reached on the World Wide Web at 
http://www.digital.com/info/internet/.
