     DIGITAL ANNOUNCES SUPPORT FOR FIRST COMMERCIALLY AVAILABLE
         64-BIT SOLUTION FOR SYBASE IQ DATA WAREHOUSE SERVER


   ...Digital Continues to Lead With 64-Bit Computing Solutions...


MAYNARD, Mass., March 26, 1996 -- Continuing its lead in delivering 
64-bit computing solutions, Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced support for Sybase IQ for the AlphaServer platform  -- 
optimized for Digital's 64-bit Alpha architecture, 64-bit Digital 
UNIX, as well as its Very Large Memory (VLM64) technology.

     Sybase IQ is designed for interactive data warehousing, and 
uses Sybase's patent-pending, Bit-Wise (TM) technology. It also uses 
advanced performance optimized algorithms for complex ad hoc queries 
to provide significant performance increases over traditional 
relational database management systems (RDBMS).  

     Today's announcement is the result of extensive collaboration 
between Sybase and Digital engineers -- working at Sybase's 
Burlington, Massachusetts facility -- to optimize Sybase IQ for 
Digital's 64-bit architecture. 

     "The level of raw performance that customers get from Sybase IQ 
running on Digital's 64-bit Alpha architecture is unmatched in the 
industry," said Jim O'Gara, Digital's vice president of Database 
Marketing Development. "Users will see the results of their complex 
queries delivered up to 500 times faster from a Digital/Sybase IQ 
solution than from traditional RDBMS solutions."

     "We are very excited to extend our relationship with Digital 
with the delivery of our next generation data warehouse Server," 
said Bruce Armstrong, Sybase vice president of Server Products.  
"Sybase IQ provides business executives with immediate access to, 
and analysis of,  complex data at speeds 5 to 500 times faster than 
a standard relational database management system. SybaseIQ, combined 
with Digital's Very Large Memory (VLM64] bit capability, will 
deliver unmatched performance for very large databases with large 
numbers of users."

     Sybase is a world-wide leader in client/server software.  
Sybase and its Powersoft division are focused on four major market 
segments: on-line transaction processing, data warehousing, mass 
deployment and electronic commerce.  Sybase's software products -- 
database, middleware and tools -- provide customers with desktop to 
enterprise solutions.  The company's mission is to provide its 
customers with an open, adaptable information systems architecture 
that enables them to develop and deliver complete information 
solutions to facilitate rapid business change.  Headquartered in 
Emeryville, Calif. Sybase is the sixth largest independent software 
company in the world. The company's Internet addresses are 
www.sybase.com and www.powersoft.com.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
