                    DIGITAL USES POWER OF 'INTRANET'
               TO CREATE UNIQUE ONLINE DISCUSSION FORUM


          Workgroup Web Forum used to create Canadian 'first'


TORONTO, ON, March 28, 1996. Digital Equipment of Canada has created a
ground-breaking Intranet-based discussion forum at the Canadian
National Internet Show using Digital's award-winning software package,
Workgroup Web Forum. Canadian National Internet Show attendees will be
able to interact with conference seminars online, participate in
conference-wide polls and discuss issues with their fellow attendees
using the power of the 'Intranet'. 

Workgroup Web Forum uses Internet technology as a flexible,
inexpensive substitute for traditional networking products to create
powerful internal networks. The Workgroup Web Forum allows users to
set up online conversations, organize them into topics, and  lets
participants add their own comments in turn. 

"Digital is excited to be involved in this Canadian first. This is an
excellent opportunity for attendees of the Canadian National Internet
Show to see the power of Intranet-based communications first hand,"
said Tyrone Lobo, Canadian Internet and Software Marketing Manager,
Digital Equipment of Canada. "Workgroup Web Forum enables
organizations and workgroups to communicate seamlessly, have virtual
discussions, and navigate through important data easily." 

One Workgroup Web Forum application will be the Internet Fitness Test.
In co-operation with Bell Global Solutions and its Sympatico Internet
service, The Globe and Mail New Media Centre, and CYBERPlex
Interactive Media, the test invites attendees to offer their input on
their own Internet habits and issues related to the Internet. The
results of this conference-wide poll will be released during the show. 

In addition, for the first time at a Canadian trade show, Workgroup
Web Forum will allow attendees to participate in the numerous
conferences taking place on Internet-related topics. Taking advantage
of Workgroup Web Forum's ability to create conference streams,
attendees will be able to form discussion groups on the topics
discussed in the seminars. 

Enhancing its ability as a conferencing tool, Workgroup Web Forum can
also access documents and allow users to comment on them. A series of
icons serve as valuable navigation aids, allowing users to access
information quickly and easily. Workgroup Web Forum employs the same
powerful search engine technology as Digital's Web search tool, Alta
Vista giving users the same advanced technology to search their
internal networks. 

Digital Equipment of Canada Limited and its partners provide industry
leading open client/server solutions to businesses across Canada.
Digital's Alpha platforms, storage products, personal computers,
networking products and services, together with industry-focused
solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win
in today's global marketplace.  In addition to offices across Canada,
the company has a major manufacturing facility in Kanata, Ontario and
a major service and support centre in Hull, Quebec. 
