announced complete enterprise messaging solutions and integration 
services for Microsoft Exchange Server, available immediately using 
Digital's Intel and Alpha systems.  Microsoft Exchange Server is the 
messaging server with integrated groupware that makes it easier to 
communicate, whether around a workgroup or around the globe.

DIGITAL SELECTS MICROSOFT EXCHANGE

     As part of Digital's commitment to business process excellence, 
the company selected Microsoft Exchange. Pilots initiated in August, 
1995, in Digital's Multivendor Customer Services organization 
validated the benefits of full-scale implementation, as well as 
providing the division with first-hand experience that will be used 
to assist customers in their own deployment.

     "Digital is internally embracing Microsoft Exchange and Windows 
NT as the core technical strategy for group connectivity, including 
enterprise messaging.  Today, over 3,000 Digital employees from 
multiple divisions in five countries are fully operational on 
Microsoft Exchange," said Dick Fishburn, CIO at Digital.  "Digital 
is committed to completing the corporate-wide Microsoft Exchange 
rollout over the next 12 months, with the goal to install over 
50,000 Microsoft Exchange clients."

MICROSOFT EXCHANGE AND THE ALLIANCE FOR ENTERPRISE COMPUTING

     "The Microsoft/Digital Alliance for Enterprise Computing (AEC) 
delivers enterprise mail solutions based on Microsoft Exchange to 
our joint customers with the speed, safety and completeness they 
have come to expect from these two industry leaders working 
together," said Jim Alchin, senior vice president of Microsoft's 
desktop and business systems division.  "Digital's investment in 
systems integration and services capabilities for the BackOffice 
Suite, coupled with its broad Intel and Alpha platform offerings, 
position Digital to deliver these solutions."

     Robert Bismuth, Digital vice president of the AEC, stated "We 
will extend the worldwide reach of Microsoft Exchange through 
Digital's strengths in systems, services, networking connectivity 
and system integration.  We are already seeing extensive customer 
demand for the combination of Microsoft Exchange and Digital 
products and services."  A demonstration of this technology is 
highlighted in the Microsoft booth at networld+interop '96, where 
they are highlighting the robust features of Microsoft Exchange  
running on Digital's Intel and Alpha servers.

MICROSOFT USES DIGITAL SERVERS TO DEMONSTRATE MICROSOFT EXCHANGE AT 
NETWORLD+INTEROP SHOW

     In Bill Gates' keynote today, he showed how Microsoft Exchange 
Server can scale from 1,500 (simulated) users to well over 10,000, 
on a single Digital server.  Digital provided Microsoft with all the 
client and server systems including its two award-winning servers, 
the Digital Prioris ZX 5133 MP Server (Intel) and the Digital 
AlphaServer 2100, to demonstrate Microsoft Exchange Server at 
Networld+Interop '96.   Microsoft chose Digital to partner in their 
booth "Scalability Wall" demo because of scalability in the Digital 
Intel and Alpha product offerings. 

CUSTOMER MOMENTUM CONTINUES TO GROW --- BRITISH COLUMBIA HYDRO 
LATEST TO SELECT MICROSOFT EXCHANGE ENVIRONMENT WITH DIGITAL  
ALPHA SERVERS

     British Columbia Hydro (BC Hydro), Canada's third largest 
electric utility, is beginning an internal pilot program to 
implement Microsoft Exchange on Digital's Alpha platform, running 
Windows NT.  Over 4,500 PCs will be involved in the migration to 
Exchange Server from IBM, Microsoft, and Macintosh messaging 
systems.

     "Choosing a vendor for Enterprise Messaging involved an 
extensive review of vendors on the market and their respective 
technical capabilities -- Digital's bid stood out because it 
understood our technical and business needs, as well as the context 
in which the Enterprise Messaging Solutions (EMS) project has to be 
delivered, " noted Larry Chow, of the EMS project at BC Hydro.  Chow 
emphasized that a key factor in selecting Microsoft Exchange Server 
was Digital's Multivendor Customer Services division for service and 
support. "Digital understands Microsoft Exchange Server because they 
have the hands-on experience gained from their installation of Microsoft 
Exchange Server in their own corporate environment."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.  
