           DIGITAL ADDS NEW ALPHA-BASED PASSIVE BACKPLANE
          SYSTEMS AND MOTHERBOARDS TO PCI PRODUCT PORTFOLIO


      -- Low-Cost PC Platform Solutions From Digital Offer OEMs
      Industrial Strength Performance, Longevity and Adherence
                        to Industry Standards


MAYNARD, Mass., April 2, 1996 -- As part of its continuing efforts 
to deliver stable, flexible solutions to its OEM customers, Digital 
Equipment Corporation today announced three additions to its line of 
PCI (peripheral component interconnect) products:  an Alpha-based 
PCI passive backplane system and the Alpha PCI 64 and Alpha PCI 164 
single board computers.  Digital's range of PCI solutions allows 
OEMs to design high-performance PC-based systems quickly and cost-
effectively with a choice of either passive backplane or motherboard 
approaches to product design.

     "As OEM market considerations such as shorter product life 
cycles and the shift from the VME to PCI standard become more 
critical, OEMs are increasingly looking toward commercial off-the-
shelf PCI products to meet their next-generation product development 
needs," said Bill Armitage, vice president of Digital's Embedded and 
Real Time OEM Products Business.  "By offering PCI-based products at 
both the modular components and motherboard level, Digital affords 
OEMs design alternatives that increase product longevity and hasten 
time-to-market."

OEMs Plan Long-Term Technology Direction Around Digital's
Modular Computing Components

     An element of Digital's line of Modular Computing Components -- 
comprised of PICMG (PCI Industrial Computer Manufacturer's Group) 
processor cards, PICMG backplanes and enclosures -- the Alpha-based 
PCI passive backplane system affords OEMs greater product design 
versatility.  OEMs have the option of either robust 64-bit RISC 
Alpha or industry standard Intel CPU architectures and can choose 
from Microsoft Windows NT, VxWorks, Digital UNIX and OpenVMS 
operating systems.

     OEMs now designing around the Intel Pentium-based PCI Passive 
Backplane system, announced in September 1995, easily can migrate 
applications to the higher performance 233 MHz Alpha-based system.  
The products' adherence to industry standards established by the 
PICMG -- a consortium of passive backplane manufacturers -- 
guarantees easy upgradability to advanced computing technology.  By 
using the passive backplane as the base platform and updating the 
processor and peripheral cards, OEMs can extend the product 
lifecycle up to five years and reduce development costs by 
approximately 20 percent annually.

     The backplane systems are available in two configurations -- 
commercial quality desktop and tower enclosures, and a rackmount 
enclosure -- to be integrated easily into either office/control room 
environments or industrial settings.

OEMs Can Swiftly and Cost-Effectively Enter Highest-Performance 
Computing Segments of the Embedded Market With New Alpha PC 
Motherboards

     For OEMs seeking rapid entry into high-performance segments of 
the embedded computing market -- data acquisition, data 
interpretation and raster image processing -- the Alpha PCI 64 and 
164 single board computers are the highest performing, most cost-
effective Alpha PC motherboards available.  These boards provide the 
ultimate in performance for compute intensive embedded applications 
with minimal risk and at low cost.

     Powered by the Alpha 21064 and 21164 microprocessors, the 
boards run at speeds of 266 MHz and 300 MHz. At 300 MHz, the 
21164-based boards are at least 90 percent faster than Intel's 
current offerings.

Pricing and Availability

     The Alpha-based PICMG single board computers are priced 
starting at $2,995.  The Intel-based systems are priced between 
$1,595 and $2,995.  The Alpha PCI 64-275 board for Windows NT with 
21064-275 MHz CPU and 2 MB of cache is priced at $2,853.  The Alpha 
PCI 164-275 board for Windows NT with 21164 MHz CPU and 2 MB of 
cache is priced at $4,218.  All are available immediately.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
