              DIGITAL SHOWS NEW 21143 PCI/CARDBUS CHIP,
        LOW-COST FAST ETHERNET SOLUTIONS AT NETWORLD+INTEROP


      ...'Network-Ready' Systems, PC Giveaway at Booth 4787...


LAS VEGAS, April 2, 1996 -- A new PCI/CardBus Fast Ethernet chip 
that lowers 100 megabit-per-second (Mbps) network solution costs for 
CardBus and network interface card (NIC) designs leads the 
Networld+Interop exhibit by Digital Semiconductor, a Digital 
Equipment Corporation business, today through Thursday at the 
Convention Center.

     Digital Semiconductor's Booth 4787, South Hall, features its 
new PCI/CardBus Fast Ethernet controller, the 21143 chip (see 
separate release), plus demonstrations of network performance, 
connectivity, and "network readiness." 

     "System and board manufacturers can discover at our booth that 
PCI Ethernet and Fast Ethernet solutions are easy and cost-effective 
to design with Digital Semiconductor's networking chips," said 
William N. Johnson, Digital Semiconductor's vice president, Sales 
and Marketing.  "Whether the target product is a PC motherboard, a 
network card, a switch, or a laptop with PC CardBus slots, our 
Ethernet/Fast Ethernet chips offer the highest level of integration 
with the most desired features at the lowest solution cost."

Digital Chip Takes on Competition

     A communications challenge pits a Digital Venturis PC, equipped 
with a 21140A PCI Fast Ethernet chip, against a network solution 
from Intel and 3Com Corporation.  The demonstration shows the 
performance advantages of Digital Semiconductor's 21140A dual-port, 
full-duplex network controller with on-chip buffers, DMA 
architecture, and energy-saving power-down modes.

     A "Connectivity-Compatibility" exhibit, linking Alpha, PowerPC, 
Intel, and Macintosh PCs in a workgroup through a Digital EtherWORKS 
100BaseTX hub, demonstrates Digital's PCI Ethernet/Fast Ethernet 
support for all major PC operating systems.

'Network-Ready' Saves Time, Money

     A "Network-Ready" display illustrates the simplicity of 
building and shipping systems with 10/100Mbps Ethernet/Fast Ethernet 
capability by mounting a 21142 chip on the motherboard and embedding 
driver software in the operating system.  The network-ready, 
"build-in" approach eliminates add-on interoperability problems, 
software loading and testing, which ultimately saves time and money 
for the manufacturer and enhances the product's value.

The Great PC Giveaway

     Booth attendees can qualify for a drawing to win a free Digital 
Venturis FP590 personal computer, complete with an installed 21140A 
chip-based Ethernet adapter card.  Entry flyers and instructions are 
available at the Digital Semiconductor booth.  Individuals who 
obtain three valid impressions from companies using Digital's 
networking chips will receive a free Digital Semiconductor baseball 
cap and qualify for the drawing. Participating companies and booth 
