             DIGITAL ANNOUNCES SIGNIFICANT ENHANCEMENTS
    TO LEADERSHIP CLIENT/SERVER ENTERPRISE-WIDE SOFTWARE FOR EDI


NEW ORLEANS, April 2, 1996 --- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced several enhancements to its UNIX version of enterprise-
wide software for Electronic Data Interchange (EDI).  Version 3.1 of 
DEC/EDI software and three new DEC/EDI application clients, unveiled 
at the 1996 DISA EC/EDI show in New Orleans, demonstrate Digital's 
continued commitment to making it easier for businesses to exchange 
EDI data in multi-platform business application and operating 
environments.  Digital introduced DEC/EDI in 1990 as the industry's 
premier client/server EDI software.  Today there are more than 600 
DEC/EDI implementations in over 40 countries worldwide.

     DEC/EDI Version 3.1 enables users to take full advantage of 
DEC/EDI's client/server architecture while running the server 
components in a UNIX environment.  It integrates a wide range of 
trading partner communications services, including X.435, X.400, 
OFTP and Bisynchronous. It also integrates EDI translation services 
for ANSI X12, UN/EDIFACT, TRADACOMS, and industry specific 
transactions, as well as application integration tools, electronic 
mail and workflow to deliver comprehensive electronic commerce 
solutions.
 
     Utilizing Digital's ObjectBroker technology to provide 
client/server interoperability, the new application clients enable 
DEC/EDI to link with business applications running in AS/400, Sun 
SPARC and IBM MVS operating environments.  In addition, the 
application clients can utilize mapping capabilities to provide 
automatic routing, delivery, and auditing of application data 
between clients. 

     According to Wayne Toye, Digital's EDI Marketing Manager, 
"We've extended our mixed platform and mixed network environments to 
support EDI client and server software for both the OpenVMS and 
Digital UNIX operating systems, and to support EDI client software 
for ten operating environments across multiple platforms.  This 
includes the three new clients as well as clients for HP-UX, IBM 
AIX, MVS-CICS, MVS-Batch and VSE-CICS."

     DEC/EDI Version 3.1 also provides enhancements to the DEC/EDI 
CommandCenter, making it easy to create and maintain DEC/EDI system 
information, EDI messages and transactions, trading partner 
profiles, mapping tables, and communications options.  Using a 
graphical user interface (GUI) running under Microsoft Windows, the 
DEC/EDI CommandCenter provides features such as cut/copy/paste, drop 
down lists, and extensive defaults that enable the EDI administrator 
to carry out all EDI configuration and development functions.

     DEC/EDI Version 3.1 and the new DEC/EDI Application Clients are 
available worldwide beginning in May.  Pricing for DEC/EDI Version 
3.1 ranges from $9,000 to $20,000 depending on system size and user 
licensing.  Pricing for the DEC/EDI CommandCenter is $2,500; and 
pricing for the DEC/EDI Application Clients ranges from $2,000 to 
$6,000. Digital provides complete solutions for implementing EDI, 
electronic commerce, and systems integration capabilities to integrate 
these solutions into business processes.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
