         DIGITAL OPENS INDUSTRY'S FIRST ENTERPRISE SOLUTIONS
                 CENTER FOR WINDOWS-BASED SOLUTIONS


             ...First of Planned Worldwide Centers from
       Microsoft/Digital Alliance for Enterprise Computing...


            ...Provides Microsoft Windows-based Solutions
                   for Multivendor Environments...


BELLEVUE, WA -- April 9, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation, as 
part of the Microsoft/Digital Alliance for Enterprise Computing, 
today opened the world's only center that supports companies 
deploying Windows NT and BackOffice solutions in a multivendor 
environment.  The new Enterprise Solutions Center for Windows(R), 
located here, will be the expertise hub for Windows NT support at 
industry and technology centers located around the world.

     The center provides the multivendor hardware and software 
environments typically found in large IT installations.  Available 
at the center are experts in client/server computing and software 
applications from Microsoft and partners.
Real-world Scenarios

     At the center, visitors can examine Windows-based applications 
working with existing software applications in prototype IT 
environments.  Visitors can use these prototypes, or build custom 
hardware and software environments, as starting points to test 
real-world scenarios for their business applications.  No other 
facility in the world offers this capability.

     Companies deploying Windows NT and BackOffice solutions in a 
multivendor environment now can gain the benefits of integrated 
consulting and technology solutions at a single location.  The 
center provides expertise in networking, client/server systems 
management, the Internet, information management, electronic 
messaging, and object-oriented application development, in addition 
to several industry-focused Windows solution prototypes.
One-Stop Shopping

     "More and more large IT installations are adding Windows NT to 
their multivendor computing environments," said Vincenzo Damiani, 
vice president and general manager of Digital's Accounts Business 
Unit.  "This center will give them the one-stop shopping they need 
to smoothly incorporate the benefits of Microsoft Windows- and 
Windows NT-based applications that support their business 
operations."

     "The Center delivers the type of integrated technology and 
services that enterprise customers require," said Bob McDowell, VP, 
Microsoft Enterprise Relationships.  "Our goal is to help customers 
meet the current and future challenges of enterprise computing by 
providing a unique setting for working out business problems with 
technology and consulting.
Cutting-Edge Competency

     "This center is yet another example of concrete benefits from 
the Microsoft/Digital Alliance for Enterprise Computing -- providing 
cutting-edge competency from the Digital/Microsoft team for 
companies using Microsoft solutions across their enterprises," said 
Robert Bismuth, Digital's vice president of the Microsoft/Digital 
Alliance for Enterprise Computing.

     The Microsoft/Digital Alliance for Enterprise Computing (AEC) 
was initiated in August 1995.  The Alliance combines Digital's 
leading multivendor support services and systems integration with 
Microsoft products and services and Digital Alpha and Intel 
products, connectivity software, and enterprise systems.  The 
Alliance enables customers to deploy business solutions on the 
Microsoft Windows and Windows NT operating systems with assurance 
of integration into the most demanding multivendor business 
environments.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
