                    DIGITAL ANNOUNCES REALIGNMENT
                        OF TWO BUSINESS UNITS
     

MAYNARD, Mass., April 10, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that its Digital Semiconductor Business Unit will 
move to the company's Components Division and that its Storage 
Business Unit will become part of its Systems Business Unit.

     "These changes better align the company's business model with 
the marketplace, enhance competitiveness and streamline our product 
distribution," said Digital Chairman Robert B. Palmer.

     The new alignment of Digital Semiconductor is designed to help 
the company expand alliances and partnerships in the growing 64-bit 
computing environment, Palmer said.

     The move of the Storage Business Unit to the Systems Business 
Unit takes advantage of the synergy between the two businesses. In 
addition, it further leverages Digital's storage technology with 
respect to Very Large Memory (VLM) architectures, as the company 
increases its leadership in the market for large-scale servers, 
Palmer said.

      Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
