          DIGITAL'S 'ALPHA PAVILION' SPOTLIGHTS TOP SYSTEMS
         FOR BROADCAST, ENTERTAINMENT INDUSTRIES AT NAB SHOW


 ...Nine Vendors Show Off Imaging, Animation, Multimedia Prowess...


LAS VEGAS, April 15, 1996 -- A lineup of the industry's most popular 
3-D imaging, animation, and video applications, running on a variety 
of systems powered by the world's highest-performance Alpha micro-
processors, highlights the exhibit by Digital Semiconductor, a 
Digital Equipment Corporation business, at this week's National 
Association of Broadcasters Conference and Exposition.

     In Booth S2612 of "Multimedia World" in the Sands Hotel 
Exposition Center, Digital Semiconductor's "Alpha Pavilion" features 
demonstrations by nine Alpha systems and software vendors, plus 
the new release of NewTek's Lightwave 5.0 3-D animation software.  
Digital Semiconductor will also demonstrate Digital FX!32 
translation software, running popular Windows applications 
including Microsoft Office 95, Microsoft Pinball, and Fury.
Alpha Boosts Creativity

     "Software vendors and users in the broadcast and entertainment 
industries are quickly discovering that Alpha-based systems offer 
the biggest boost to creativity and productivity through superior 
