          DIGITAL INTRODUCES THREE NEW ALPHASTUDIO PRODUCTS
               TO BE SHOWCASED AT 1996 NAB CONFERENCE


          AlphaStudio Software, AlphaStudio Content Server
         and AlphaStudio Rev Station Provide Foundation for
                Creating Digital Broadcast Solutions


LAS VEGAS, NV, April 15, 1996 -- Streamlining the migration from 
analog to digital broadcast video, Digital Equipment Corporation 
today introduced three new products that comprise the architecture 
of Digital's AlphaStudio Broadcast System, an industry-leading, 
digital-based broadcast video solution.  The three components, the 
AlphaStudio Broadcast System Software, AlphaStudio Content Server 
and AlphaStudio Rev Station, are designed to fully integrate all 
the components of Digital's highly reliable digital broadcast video
system with a building-block approach.

     The new AlphaStudio components are being demonstrated at the 
National Association of Broadcasting (NAB) Conference in Las Vegas, 
April 16-18.  Conference attendees may visit the Digital booth 
(5053) to view the complete system, including the AlphaStudio 
Software, Content Server and REV Station. "Digital is providing 
broadcasters with a digital video solutions that delivers video over 
a network and helps broadcasters contain operating costs,"said Gene 
Nelson, Digital's vice president, worldwide Custom Systems 
Solutions. "Digital's new AlphaStudio components -- the AlphaStudio 
Content Server, REV Station and AlphaStudio Broadcast Systems software -- 
compliment Digital's base AlphaStudio Broadcast System to provide a 
comprehensive, open digital video solution for broadcasters." 

The Components

     The AlphaStudio Broadcast System Software provides modular 
software architecture that precisely manages and controls the 
location and movement of digital video data.  The three software 
modules in the system, a storage, video and control module, run in 
the 64-bit RISC Alpha, Digital UNIX environment.  UNIX provides the 
power and stability necessary to run in broadcast environments 
today. Compatible with the industry-standard Master Control 
Automation products external to the AlphaStudio system, the 
AlphaStudio Software interfaces with the Louth Automation protocol 
and has tools for managing the digital environment.

     The AlphaStudio Content Server eliminates the need for analog 
video tape in broadcast operations by replacing the analog video 
cart with digital disk and tape archives.  These storage servers can 
be interconnected with high-bandwidth FDDI technology.

     The AlphaStudio REV Station is a direct digital replacement for 
analog VTRs, making the migration from analog to digital immediate.  
Seamlessly integrating with the AlphaStudio Broadcast System or on 
its own, the AlphaStudio REV Station stores from 35 minutes to nine 
hours of broadcast quality video.  Easy to install and configure, it 
can support multiple bi-directional audio/video channels, which are 
simultaneously able to access video storage. The AlphaStudio REV 
Station's network connectivity options include Ethernet, FDDI or ATM 
and optional components provide support for NTSC and PAL inputs and 
outputs.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions form personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
