          DIGITAL AND MICROSOFT TO EXTEND ENTERPRISE REACH
                       OF MICROSOFT SQL SERVER

         
          ...Announce development and testing of Very Large
                     Database systems (VLDB)...


MAYNARD, Mass., April 16, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it is joining with Microsoft Corporation to 
develop and test Very Large Database (VLDB) systems for Microsoft 
SQL Server at Microsoft's corporate campus in Redmond, Wash.

     The VLDB testing will include Digital's RISC-based AlphaServer 
systems and Intel-based Prioris servers, which currently are part of 
the Microsoft SQL Server test lab in Redmond.

     Digital also will provide StorageWorks RAID subsystems for 
development and testing of Microsoft SQL Server databases. The 
StorageWorks subsystem will include RAID Array Controllers and Disk 
Drives for a one-half terabyte (500 GB) Windows NT Server and 
Microsoft SQL Server configuration.

     In addition, Digital announced that it will provide high 
availability support for Microsoft SQL Server 6.5 through the 
Digital Clusters for Windows NT product, which will be available 
this summer. Digital Clusters for Windows NT software will support 
database fail-over for Microsoft SQL Server 6.5.

     "Today's announcements provide further evidence of the ongoing, 
close collaboration between Digital and Microsoft," said Robert 
Bismuth, Digital vice president of the Microsoft Alliance for 
Enterprise Computing. "By offering customers the benefits of a VLDB 
testing that employs the world's most powerful servers, our 
breakthrough StorageWorks subsystems, and the experience of the 
industry's clustering technology pioneer, we will help Microsoft 
extend the reach of Microsoft SQL Server even further into the 
enterprise," said Bismuth.

     Just last week, Digital opened the new Enterprise Solutions 
Center for Windows in Bellevue, Wash., where customers and business 
partners can work with Digital and Microsoft experts to optimize 
their Microsoft Windows-based enterprise solutions.

     "The Microsoft and Digital VLDB development and testing effort, 
using Digital StorageWorks components, will help us proactively 
anticipate customer needs and improve the ability of Microsoft SQL 
Server to handle databases of 512 gigabytes and more," said Jim 
Ewel, group product manager, SQL Server, at Microsoft. "This new 
initiative greatly extends our joint efforts to offer customers 
using AlphaServer and Prioris systems the most advanced, flexible 
database capabilities on the market, with plenty of headroom for the 
future."

PR Newswire Manages Growth with Alpha and Microsoft SQL Server

     With an expanding worldwide client base of 17,000, PR Newswire, 
of New York City, distributes as many as two million pages of news 
releases by fax per month, in addition to nearly 500 releases per 
day on the Newswire. To manage this growth, PR Newswire depends on 
client/server computing with Digital AlphaServer systems and 
Microsoft SQL Server technology.

     Pascal Mattiocco, vice president of information technology at 
PR Newswire, said, "The synergy between Microsoft and Digital is 
very strong. It's a natural match: the performance of Digital's 
AlphaServer systems and the and easy maintenance and performance of 
Microsoft SQL Server. We have the client/server solution we need now 
and in the future."

     Microsoft/Digital Alliance for Enterprise Computing (AEC) was 
initiated in August 1995.  The Alliance combines Digital's leading 
multivendor support services and systems integration with Microsoft 
products and services and Digital Alpha and Intel products, 
connectivity software, and enterprise systems. The Alliance enables 
customers to deploy business solutions on the Microsoft Windows and 
Windows NT operating systems and integrate them into the most 
demanding multivendor business environments.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. See the AlphaServer Web site 
at:  www.digital.com/info/alphaserver
