                 DIGITAL INCREASES ITS LEADERSHIP IN
                  ENTERPRISE MESSAGING CONNECTIVITY


     ...New offerings highlighted by enhanced software solutions
                  and worldwide services support...


ANAHEIM, Calif., April 29, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation, 
the industry leader in mail connectivity, today announced an 
enhanced suite of solutions that make it easier for companies to 
transport and manage information across heterogeneous electronic 
mail systems.  This new solutions portfolio which is available 
immediately includes both software and services, is cost-effective, 
protects existing investments, and provides an easy migration path 
to the newest offerings such as Microsoft Exchange Server.

Highlights of today's announcement are:

     o 	Enhanced software solutions, including new Internet 
        capabilities providing low-cost Web publishing and worldwide 
        access to multiformat documents via Web browsers, as well as 
        new versions of Digital X.500 Directory Services, MAILbus 
        400 Messaging Transfer Agent, MAILbus Monitor Systems 
        Management, and ALL-IN-1 Office Server.

     o 	A new range of worldwide enterprise messaging services 
        providing migration, integration, and upgrade capabilities.
       	These new services include a new program - 'Moving to 
        Microsoft Exchange' - for customers wishing to implement 
        Microsoft Exchange Server, Microsoft's messaging server with 
        integrated groupware, in their enterprise messaging 
        environment.

     "We believe that most large enterprises will continue to 
operate with multivendor messaging environments for at least the 
next several years.  Today's announcement underscores our expertise 
in providing connectivity in multiplatform customer environments," 
said Wes Melling, vice president of the OpenVMS Business Unit at 
Digital Equipment Corporation.  "With our newly expanded portfolio 
of offerings, Digital and its business partners deliver standards-
based, enterprise-wide messaging infrastructures for high volume, 
mission-critical message delivery."   

Enhanced Messaging Solutions

     Digital X.500 Directory Services V3.0 provides users with a 
single, robust, easy-to-use and maintain directory source that 
adheres to the latest X.500 standard. This newest version of 
Digital's X.500 will be DMS (Defense Messaging System) compliant.  
It is the fastest in the industry, with speeds of 10 milliseconds 
per directory service read, or 200 operations per second.  The new 
version adds interfaces to NetScape, Mosaic, LDAP (Lightweight 
Directory Access Protocol), and other directory service providers.  
In addition, Digital X.500 Directory Services also offers 
connectivity to ALL-IN-1 and Microsoft Exchange directories, as well 
as  support for very large databases - containing millions of 
entries per server - and usage-based pricing, with the pricing based 
on the number of entries in a server. 				    

     Digital's MAILbus 400 Message Transfer Agent (MTA) V2.0 
provides connectivity for Microsoft Exchange Server to ALL-IN-1, 
MailWorks, and non-Digital mail systems. The new version also provides 
access to Mastersoft's Document Converter Library which gives users 
the ability to convert documents to any format required by the recipient. 
Usage Licensing for MAILbus 400 MTA allows users to control costs by 
selecting the appropriate license, based on message traffic level.

     MAILbus Monitor V2.0 monitors messaging systems and network 
applications across WAN and LAN networks from a central point. This 
management tool highlights problems and potential problems before 
they affect the network.

     With the introduction of ALL-IN-1 V3.2, users now have access 
to an ALL-IN-1 solution capable of running solely on a Digital 
Alpha-based system.  New World Wide Web capabilities redefine 
ALL-IN-1 V3.2 as an Intranet and Internet publishing vehicle 
offering low cost Web publishing without the need for HTML authoring 
tools.  The new version also provides MAPI 1 Client support and 
direct access to X.400 and X.500.  				    

Global Services

     Digital now offers a full suite of messaging connectivity 
solutions designed to give users choices in desktop, server, 
enterprise messaging backbone and operating system.  Services 
offered by Systems Integrations Services and Multivendor Customer 
Services include:

     o 	Enterprise Messaging Implementation Service which helps 
        users build a complete, standards-based enterprise messaging 
       	solution.
  
     o 	ALL-IN-1 Upgrade Services which assists users in moving to 
        an all Alpha-based messaging solution.  		    

     o 	'Moving to Microsoft Exchange' which is a new program 
        comprised of services for customers who plan to implement 
        Microsoft Exchange Server, either within their existing 
        messaging environment, or as a complete enterprise messaging 
        solution.
    
     o 	The Directory Synchronization service which provides fully 
        automated synchronization of disparate directories from 
        multiple vendors.
    
     These services will be provided by a global network of newly 
established Integrated Solutions Teams.				    

     "We are pleased to be affiliated with Digital, who is bringing 
its extensive messaging expertise to provide services and support 
for Microsoft Exchange Server," said Greg Lobdell, Group Product 
Manager, Messaging and Groupware at Microsoft Corporation.  "Digital 
is uniquely positioned to provide a well-planned implementation of 
enterprise wide messaging that integrates Microsoft Exchange Server 
into the most complex messaging environments."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
